field, While/if-errorlevel control). Speed fix: sets solve in forked processes (group_by_set + ProcessPoolExecutor, sequential fallback); the nested-zip index no longer decrypts every script leaf just to sniff for PK (375 PBKDF2s -> only the members asked, per set, in parallel); powerplay.xor is one big-int XOR.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: none in the bytes (D8 Mastery 7432c509, re-flagged on D23). It is permanently UNVERIFIABLE: the D8 attempt EXPIRED (no GM grade), so expected.json stays {}. The D23 solver's 3075 answers equal the D8 solver's submission (mastery/attempts/7432c509/last_timed.json) 3075/3075, and that solver's other D8 Mastery runs were GM-verified. The real failure was SPEED: ~1100 serial AES PBKDF2s on the D23 Mastery bundle. Rule: the WinZip-AES salt sits right after each local header, so derive every member key up front in a thread pool (OpenSSL PBKDF2 releases the GIL) and look it up in the pyzipper PBKDF2 patch (solve.py `_prefetch_keys`/`_KEYS`). Profiled time dropped from 9.8 s to 5.1 s on auto-mastery-e24c070d; answers unchanged.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- `lib.common.gm_error_body(artdir) -> bytes|None`: detect a GM error JSON (`rate_limited`, ...) saved in place of an\n  artifact, so every solver fails loudly. Better still: the harness download step (hctf/hb_timed.py) should retry on\n  `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` and never save it as the artifact. That would have saved this timed attempt.\n- `lib.common.iter_entries(root, leaf_ext=...)`: don't load a member just to sniff for a nested zip when its name has a script/text extension (.js/.ps1/.py/.vbs/.cmd/.bat/.sh/.mjs/.php/...). Today it decrypts every AES member of a Mastery bundle up front (375 PBKDF2 = ~0.2 s locally, many times that on Homebase), and each forked set repeats it. See `_iter_entries` in this solve.py.\n- `lib.common._zip_open`: prefetch WinZip-AES keys for all members in parallel (salt = bytes after the local header; `hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac` in a ThreadPoolExecutor), as D23 solve.py `_prefetch_keys` does. Every script-lane Mastery solver pays ~1 ms x members serially today.\n- `lib.codec`: ~295 module-level `re.compile`s cost ~0.3 s per solver start, and `_find_codecs_uncached` runs ~16 regex probes per text (4669 searches / 287 texts = 0.4 s on the D23 Mastery). Compile lazily and gate each detector on a cheap substring test (`'Codec_' in text`, ...).\n----\n20 challenges/day24/scripting-web-of-lies/solver/NOTES.md\nchallenges/day24/scripting-web-of-lies/solver:\nNOTES.md\n__pycache__\nbashplan.py\nbatchplan.py\ncases\njsdecode.js\npowerplay.py\npyplan.py\nsolve.py\nvbsplan.py\n\nchallenges/day24/scripting-web-of-lies/solver/cases:\nauto-mastery-1478867c\nauto-mastery-1dfd4cf6\nauto-mastery-2620b793\nauto-mastery-2afec5c3\nauto-mastery-2c52d50f\nauto-mastery-2d722b36\nauto-mastery-42610860\nauto-mastery-4d9ad8d7\nauto-mastery-635241de\nauto-mastery-65cb0a01\nauto-mastery-78b00cf3\nauto-mastery-7a1c517e\nauto-mastery-7fbfc526\nauto-mastery-81bb44e6\nauto-mastery-8a650537\nauto-mastery-93477ae4\nauto-mastery-955f8056\nauto-mastery-b585de66\nauto-mastery-c8d60ca4\nauto-mastery-e24c070d\nauto-time_trial-0df5072d\nauto-time_trial-19325d49\nauto-time_trial-1c3f64b8\nauto-time_trial-2a76a105\nauto-time_trial-3ecccc6e\nauto-time_trial-516aa6d1\nauto-time_trial-717b8371\nauto-time_trial-9bf550a3\nauto-time_trial-a719c002\nauto-time_trial-b10c4da4\nauto-time_trial-b7cd2e36\nauto-time_trial-c355207f\nauto-time_trial-c474d1d8\nauto-time_trial-c739141b\nauto-time_trial-d629142e\nauto-time_trial-dfcfb51e\nauto-time_trial-e3b3b2d1\nauto-time_trial-f01e0ff9\nauto-time_trial-f1f48f56\nauto-time_trial-f99ea9ec\ncompound-d15-auto-mastery-7fbfc526\ncompound-merge-d23\nmastery-e24c070d\nsingle_solve\ntime_trial-b10c4da4\nvariant-mastery-7432c509\nvariant-mastery-7fbfc526\nvariant-mastery-e24c070d\nvariant-time_trial-49b73141\nvariant-time_trial-5ab8013f\nvariant-time_trial-7d6f8d53\nvariant-time_trial-b10c4da4\n{\n  \"base\": \"script-analysis-day-24-jsp-web