{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0131QW87tCzatDbjHtvnRPDo","type":"tool_result","content":"236\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..GDScript).\n237\tEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER (D16, D23 \"level that doesn't belong\": plan_canonical) / CI (D21) / INSTALLER (D22) prompts: flavour.\n238\t```\n239\t\n240\t## Readiness gaps\n241\tBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D21 nights (see git history) and D22 night\n242\tinstaller-action-model, nsis-string-define-fold, inno-setup-iss-route, wix-msi-custom-action-route,\n243\tnsis-compiled-installer-extract, package-manager-install-manifests, electron-asar-squirrel-route, cloud-iac-userdata-route,\n244\tyaml-scalar-carrier-twists. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router,\n245\tfile-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS\n246\t(stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D24:\n247\twhat actually cost D23 (timed per-file contract grammar in lib, tag-directed LYR peel with wider layer names, corpus\n248\tcross-file / stage-chain correlation incl. the never-asked \"level that doesn't belong\", field-keyed composite labels), then the\n249\ttitle thread (game-engine script languages, Godot resources/packs, game archives), then the installer leftovers.\n250\t\n251\t```json\n252\t[\n253\t  {\"id\": \"per-file-hashed-contract\", \"concept\": \"timed per-file contract grammar: `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` ids over `<6hex>.<ext>` members with composite / derived fields\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery reshaped the contract (single kept semantic ids); the carried solver answered 593/1495. Move D23 solve.py PF_ID/pf_value into lib: lib.codec.pf_route(answer_id, question, members)->(family, member, field); pf_answer(field, plan, question, kind)-> value for composite style (JS function|invocation|property, batch graph|control|expansion, VBS representation|transform|control), python carrier (carrier|windows_chain) and obfuscation (syntax|obfuscation), indicator by the precedence list PARSED FROM THE QUESTION TEXT (not hard-coded), campaign-token (after first hyphen), url-host, path-leaf, PS secondary/tertiary keyed by scenario. Also accept unknown 4-8 hex stems and future fields via plan_answer. Test on challenges/day23/scripting-press-start-to-decode/solver/cases/variant-time_trial-b10c4da4 and variant-mastery-e24c070d (GM-verified).\"},\n254\t  {\"id\": \"lyr-tag-layer-peel\", \"concept\": \"tag-directed layered carrier peel: `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l1>_<l2>_..-<data>` with today's and likely next layer names\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 timed tags listed ENCODE layers from {b64,b32,hex,rev,frag} (1-3 deep, 54 combos); obfuscation answer = the layer string. Put lib.codec.lyr_peel(tag, data) in lib with tolerant names for the next 'power-up': b64u/urlsafe, b32hex, b58, b85/a85/z85, gz/gzip, zlib/deflate, bz2, xz/lzma, rot13/rotN, xor<hex>, url/pct, uu, qp, utf16, rev, frag; up to 6 layers; a tag mismatch falls back to shape peel; accept only v=. Wire into v3_plan so SPLIT arrays carrying a LYR head (D23 Apps Script) also peel.\"},\n255\t  {\"id\": \"corpus-stage-correlation\", \"concept\": \"corpus cross-file correlation: precursor->next-stage links, handoff ids, stage chains, and the odd member out\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 asked `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` that invoke-python-stage.ps1 passes to that .py (`$NextStage`, `--handoff-id` ArgumentVector); Mastery lost 6 ids by resolving it across sets. Prompt: 'correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus to find the level that doesn't belong'. Build lib.codec.corpus_links(members:{name: text}, plans) -> edges (src, dst, via: next_stage|file_path|handoff_id|next_language|url) scoped to ONE set, link_value(dst, key) for 'what does X pass to Y' questions, and stage_outlier(plans, edges) -> member whose declared next_language/stage_count/stage_profile/steps disagree with its siblings or whose link target is missing; answers in original spelling.\"},\n256\t  {\"id\": \"game-script-language-route\", \"concept\": \"game-engine / modding script languages as the next v=3 polyglot (Luau, Ren'Py, GML, Squirrel, AngelScript, Pawn, mcfunction, UnrealScript, Unity C#, LÖVE Lua)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 'Press Start to Decode' / base game-resource-loader = GDScript; the lane adds one sibling per thread (AutoIt->AHK, Jenkins->GHA). Fixture battery per language with the D8 4-file polyglot shape, verify lib.codec.v3_plan reads each comment/descriptor form: Luau `-- ` + `local DESCRIPTOR_X: string = \\\"..\\\"`; Ren'Py `# ` + `define descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"` / `$ x = ..` in `init python:`; GML `// ` + `#macro DESCRIPTOR_X \\\"..\\\"` / `global.x = ..`; Squirrel `// ` + `local x = @\\\"..\\\"` (verbatim, `\\\"\\\"` escape); AngelScript `const string x = ..`; Pawn `new const x[] = \\\"..\\\"` + `\\\\` escapes; mcfunction `# ` + `data modify storage huntress:x set value \\\"..\\\"`; UnrealScript `var string x; defaultproperties { x=\\\"..\\\" }`; Unity C# `[SerializeField] string x = ..`.\"},\n257\t  {\"id\": \"godot-resource-pck-carrier\", \"concept\": \"Godot resource containers: `.tscn`/`.tres` embedded GDScript (`script/source = \\\"..\\\"`), `.pck` packs, `.gdc` tokenized scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A 'resource loader' twist would move the D23 .gd into a Godot resource: `[sub_resource type=\\\"GDScript\\\" id=..]` with `script/source = \\\"<escaped source>\\\"` (escapes \\\\n \\\\t \\\\\\\" ) -> nested-carrier unescape then V3_MARK. `.pck`: magic GDPC, u32 pack ver, engine ver, reserved, file count, entries (path len+path, offset u64, size u64, md5) -> extract text members (.gd/.tscn/.tres/.cfg/.json) without running anything; `.gdc` (Godot 3 tokenized) -> string-table extract. lib.codec.godot_members(data)->[(path, bytes)].\"},\n258\t  {\"id\": \"game-archive-carriers\", \"concept\": \"other game archives as script carriers: Ren'Py `.rpa`/`.rpyc`, LÖVE `.love`, Unity TextAsset bundles, RPG Maker `plugins.js`\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"`.rpa` RPA-3.0 header `RPA-3.0 <hexoffset> <hexkey>` -> zlib-compressed pickle index (offset/len XOR key) -- parse with a RESTRICTED pickle reader that allows only dict/list/tuple/str/bytes/int (no find_class); `.rpyc` `RENPY RPC2` slot table -> zlib chunk -> string literals only (no unpickle of AST classes). `.love` = zip of .lua; Unity `UnityFS` bundle -> LZ4 blocks -> TextAsset strings (scan for HUNTRESS markers); RPG Maker `js/plugins.js` `$plugins = [..]`. Output: [(path, text)] for the marker scan.\"},\n259\t  {\"id\": \"composite-label-field-regime\", \"concept\": \"synthetic labels keyed by the asking FIELD (composite `-style` triple vs stand-alone field)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23: batch `call set \\\"..%%x%%..\\\"` = call_double inside `graph|control|expansion` (TT 4 + Mastery 12 ids rejected as percent) but percent in the stand-alone `-expansion` field. Extend lib.codec.label_expansion(construct, regime, field=) with a field axis and a tabulator: label_table(cases_dir) -> {(construct, field, regime): {label: n}} from expected.json + gm_feedback.json, flagging any construct whose label differs by field; same treatment for JS styles and VBS control inside composites.\"},\n260\t  {\"id\": \"linux-package-maintainer-scripts\", \"concept\": \"deb / rpm / PKGBUILD / APKBUILD maintainer scripts as installer-chain carriers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Linux side of 'installer script chain'. pkg_scripts(name, data)->[{format, hook (preinst|postinst|prerm|postrm|config|triggers|%pre|%post|%preun|%postun|%pretrans|%posttrans|%trigger*|pre_install|post_install|post_upgrade), interpreter, body}]: `.deb` = ar (`!<arch>\\\\n`, 60-byte headers) -> `control.tar.gz|xz|zst` (tarfile handles gz/xz; zst -> report) -> scripts; `.rpm` = 96-byte lead `ED AB EE DB`, signature header (8-byte aligned) then main header (`8E AD E8 01`, index entries tag/type/offset/count) -> tags PREIN 1023, POSTIN 1024, PREUN 1025, POSTUN 1026, PREINPROG 1085.., TRIGGERSCRIPTS 1065, PRETRANS 1151, POSTTRANS 1152; `.spec` text `%post -p /bin/sh` sections; Arch `PKGBUILD` `install=x.install` + `post_install() {..}`; Alpine `.pre-install`/`.post-install`. Bodies -> bash/python route + marker scan. ATT&CK T1546.016 (installer packages), T1059.004. Gate: in-test built ar/tar + minimal rpm header fixtures; D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n261\t  {\"id\": \"macos-pkg-installer-scripts\", \"concept\": \"macOS flat `.pkg` (xar) Distribution JavaScript and preinstall/postinstall scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Installer sibling on macOS (cf. D13 AppleScript). macpkg_scripts(data)->[{path, kind (distribution_js|preinstall|postinstall|payload), lang, body}]: xar header (`xar!`, u16 header size, u16 version, u64 toc_len_compressed, u64 toc_len_uncompressed, u32 checksum alg), zlib TOC XML -> <file> entries with <data><offset><length><encoding style=application/x-gzip|x-bzip2>, heap after TOC; `Distribution` XML `<installer-gui-script>` `<script>` CDATA JS (`system.run('/bin/sh', ..)`, `installation-check`/`volume-check` functions) -> JS route; `Scripts` member = gzip cpio (odc `070707` / newc `070701`) -> preinstall/postinstall shebang -> bash/python/osascript route. ATT&CK T1546.016, T1059.002/.004/.007. Gate: in-test built xar + cpio fixtures (pure stdlib zlib/gzip); D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n262\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values.\"},\n263\t  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens).\"},\n264\t  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D22: the D22 solve.py (byte-identical D21 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n265\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n266\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n267\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n268\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n269\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n270\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file.\"},\n271\t  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n272\t  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n273\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n274\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n275\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n276\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n277\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n278\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n279\t]\n280\t```"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"278d30c6-8338-440c-a01b-243a15881645","uuid":"ff82587c-1bf0-4e45-a681-5df0def82a5c","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:21:14.174Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md","content":" .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..GDScript).\nEQUIVALENCE/OUTLIER (D16, D23 \"level that doesn't belong\": plan_canonical) / CI (D21) / INSTALLER (D22) prompts: flavour.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D21 nights (see git history) and D22 night\ninstaller-action-model, nsis-string-define-fold, inno-setup-iss-route, wix-msi-custom-action-route,\nnsis-compiled-installer-extract, package-manager-install-manifests, electron-asar-squirrel-route, cloud-iac-userdata-route,\nyaml-scalar-carrier-twists. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router,\nfile-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS\n(stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D24:\nwhat actually cost D23 (timed per-file contract grammar in lib, tag-directed LYR peel with wider layer names, corpus\ncross-file / stage-chain correlation incl. the never-asked \"level that doesn't belong\", field-keyed composite labels), then the\ntitle thread (game-engine script languages, Godot resources/packs, game archives), then the installer leftovers.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"per-file-hashed-contract\", \"concept\": \"timed per-file contract grammar: `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` ids over `<6hex>.<ext>` members with composite / derived fields\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT/Mastery reshaped the contract (single kept semantic ids); the carried solver answered 593/1495. Move D23 solve.py PF_ID/pf_value into lib: lib.codec.pf_route(answer_id, question, members)->(family, member, field); pf_answer(field, plan, question, kind)-> value for composite style (JS function|invocation|property, batch graph|control|expansion, VBS representation|transform|control), python carrier (carrier|windows_chain) and obfuscation (syntax|obfuscation), indicator by the precedence list PARSED FROM THE QUESTION TEXT (not hard-coded), campaign-token (after first hyphen), url-host, path-leaf, PS secondary/tertiary keyed by scenario. Also accept unknown 4-8 hex stems and future fields via plan_answer. Test on challenges/day23/scripting-press-start-to-decode/solver/cases/variant-time_trial-b10c4da4 and variant-mastery-e24c070d (GM-verified).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lyr-tag-layer-peel\", \"concept\": \"tag-directed layered carrier peel: `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l1>_<l2>_..-<data>` with today's and likely next layer names\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 timed tags listed ENCODE layers from {b64,b32,hex,rev,frag} (1-3 deep, 54 combos); obfuscation answer = the layer string. Put lib.codec.lyr_peel(tag, data) in lib with tolerant names for the next 'power-up': b64u/urlsafe, b32hex, b58, b85/a85/z85, gz/gzip, zlib/deflate, bz2, xz/lzma, rot13/rotN, xor<hex>, url/pct, uu, qp, utf16, rev, frag; up to 6 layers; a tag mismatch falls back to shape peel; accept only v=. Wire into v3_plan so SPLIT arrays carrying a LYR head (D23 Apps Script) also peel.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"corpus-stage-correlation\", \"concept\": \"corpus cross-file correlation: precursor->next-stage links, handoff ids, stage chains, and the odd member out\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 asked `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` that invoke-python-stage.ps1 passes to that .py (`$NextStage`, `--handoff-id` ArgumentVector); Mastery lost 6 ids by resolving it across sets. Prompt: 'correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus to find the level that doesn't belong'. Build lib.codec.corpus_links(members:{name: text}, plans) -> edges (src, dst, via: next_stage|file_path|handoff_id|next_language|url) scoped to ONE set, link_value(dst, key) for 'what does X pass to Y' questions, and stage_outlier(plans, edges) -> member whose declared next_language/stage_count/stage_profile/steps disagree with its siblings or whose link target is missing; answers in original spelling.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"game-script-language-route\", \"concept\": \"game-engine / modding script languages as the next v=3 polyglot (Luau, Ren'Py, GML, Squirrel, AngelScript, Pawn, mcfunction, UnrealScript, Unity C#, LÖVE Lua)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 'Press Start to Decode' / base game-resource-loader = GDScript; the lane adds one sibling per thread (AutoIt->AHK, Jenkins->GHA). Fixture battery per language with the D8 4-file polyglot shape, verify lib.codec.v3_plan reads each comment/descriptor form: Luau `-- ` + `local DESCRIPTOR_X: string = \\\"..\\\"`; Ren'Py `# ` + `define descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"` / `$ x = ..` in `init python:`; GML `// ` + `#macro DESCRIPTOR_X \\\"..\\\"` / `global.x = ..`; Squirrel `// ` + `local x = @\\\"..\\\"` (verbatim, `\\\"\\\"` escape); AngelScript `const string x = ..`; Pawn `new const x[] = \\\"..\\\"` + `\\\\` escapes; mcfunction `# ` + `data modify storage huntress:x set value \\\"..\\\"`; UnrealScript `var string x; defaultproperties { x=\\\"..\\\" }`; Unity C# `[SerializeField] string x = ..`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-resource-pck-carrier\", \"concept\": \"Godot resource containers: `.tscn`/`.tres` embedded GDScript (`script/source = \\\"..\\\"`), `.pck` packs, `.gdc` tokenized scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A 'resource loader' twist would move the D23 .gd into a Godot resource: `[sub_resource type=\\\"GDScript\\\" id=..]` with `script/source = \\\"<escaped source>\\\"` (escapes \\\\n \\\\t \\\\\\\" ) -> nested-carrier unescape then V3_MARK. `.pck`: magic GDPC, u32 pack ver, engine ver, reserved, file count, entries (path len+path, offset u64, size u64, md5) -> extract text members (.gd/.tscn/.tres/.cfg/.json) without running anything; `.gdc` (Godot 3 tokenized) -> string-table extract. lib.codec.godot_members(data)->[(path, bytes)].\"},\n  {\"id\": \"game-archive-carriers\", \"concept\": \"other game archives as script carriers: Ren'Py `.rpa`/`.rpyc`, LÖVE `.love`, Unity TextAsset bundles, RPG Maker `plugins.js`\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"`.rpa` RPA-3.0 header `RPA-3.0 <hexoffset> <hexkey>` -> zlib-compressed pickle index (offset/len XOR key) -- parse with a RESTRICTED pickle reader that allows only dict/list/tuple/str/bytes/int (no find_class); `.rpyc` `RENPY RPC2` slot table -> zlib chunk -> string literals only (no unpickle of AST classes). `.love` = zip of .lua; Unity `UnityFS` bundle -> LZ4 blocks -> TextAsset strings (scan for HUNTRESS markers); RPG Maker `js/plugins.js` `$plugins = [..]`. Output: [(path, text)] for the marker scan.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"composite-label-field-regime\", \"concept\": \"synthetic labels keyed by the asking FIELD (composite `-style` triple vs stand-alone field)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23: batch `call set \\\"..%%x%%..\\\"` = call_double inside `graph|control|expansion` (TT 4 + Mastery 12 ids rejected as percent) but percent in the stand-alone `-expansion` field. Extend lib.codec.label_expansion(construct, regime, field=) with a field axis and a tabulator: label_table(cases_dir) -> {(construct, field, regime): {label: n}} from expected.json + gm_feedback.json, flagging any construct whose label differs by field; same treatment for JS styles and VBS control inside composites.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"linux-package-maintainer-scripts\", \"concept\": \"deb / rpm / PKGBUILD / APKBUILD maintainer scripts as installer-chain carriers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Linux side of 'installer script chain'. pkg_scripts(name, data)->[{format, hook (preinst|postinst|prerm|postrm|config|triggers|%pre|%post|%preun|%postun|%pretrans|%posttrans|%trigger*|pre_install|post_install|post_upgrade), interpreter, body}]: `.deb` = ar (`!<arch>\\\\n`, 60-byte headers) -> `control.tar.gz|xz|zst` (tarfile handles gz/xz; zst -> report) -> scripts; `.rpm` = 96-byte lead `ED AB EE DB`, signature header (8-byte aligned) then main header (`8E AD E8 01`, index entries tag/type/offset/count) -> tags PREIN 1023, POSTIN 1024, PREUN 1025, POSTUN 1026, PREINPROG 1085.., TRIGGERSCRIPTS 1065, PRETRANS 1151, POSTTRANS 1152; `.spec` text `%post -p /bin/sh` sections; Arch `PKGBUILD` `install=x.install` + `post_install() {..}`; Alpine `.pre-install`/`.post-install`. Bodies -> bash/python route + marker scan. ATT&CK T1546.016 (installer packages), T1059.004. Gate: in-test built ar/tar + minimal rpm header fixtures; D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"macos-pkg-installer-scripts\", \"concept\": \"macOS flat `.pkg` (xar) Distribution JavaScript and preinstall/postinstall scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Installer sibling on macOS (cf. D13 AppleScript). macpkg_scripts(data)->[{path, kind (distribution_js|preinstall|postinstall|payload), lang, body}]: xar header (`xar!`, u16 header size, u16 version, u64 toc_len_compressed, u64 toc_len_uncompressed, u32 checksum alg), zlib TOC XML -> <file> entries with <data><offset><length><encoding style=application/x-gzip|x-bzip2>, heap after TOC; `Distribution` XML `<installer-gui-script>` `<script>` CDATA JS (`system.run('/bin/sh', ..)`, `installation-check`/`volume-check` functions) -> JS route; `Scripts` member = gzip cpio (odc `070707` / newc `070701`) -> preinstall/postinstall shebang -> bash/python/osascript route. ATT&CK T1546.016, T1059.002/.004/.007. Gate: in-test built xar + cpio fixtures (pure stdlib zlib/gzip); D1-D22 unchanged.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scope\", \"concept\": \"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"timed-contract-shape-diff\", \"concept\": \"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OPEN after D22: the D22 solve.py (byte-identical D21 copy) has no lib.codec.v3_plan / inner_scripts call (D20-D22 needed none because every carrier was plain). Do it in the next solver-authoring pass.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `polyglot-csharp_script` (campaign CSHARP_SCRIPT-, url host csharp_script-..) and host `host-aspx-inline-csharp-csharp-script` (profile aspx_inline_csharp, file extension .csx although the bytes are an ASPX page). D20: `polyglot-groovy` (campaign GROOVY-), hosts `host-jenkins-pipeline-groovy` (profile jenkins_pipeline) and `host-classic-asp-vbscript` (profile classic_asp, language vbscript, campaign VBSCRIPT-, file .vbs although the bytes are an ASP page). D21: `polyglot-github_actions` (campaign GITHUB_ACTIONS-, url host github_actions-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-github_actions/..), no host file. D22: `polyglot-nsis` (campaign NSIS-, url host nsis-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-nsis/..), no host file.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"godot-re-tools\", \"concept\": \"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"unrpyc\", \"concept\": \"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D19 shipped .csx source only (static read was enough). Install dotnet-script only if a csx variant needs `#load`/`#r` resolution: dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script (parse only; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild/Assembly.Load payloads).\"}\n]\n```","numLines":45,"startLine":236,"totalLines":281}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0131QW87tCzatDbjHtvnRPDo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
