{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgM8yWHgSSTt2M1wTXWx4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HAb6NkdahsfmhLNpGHiS42","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\nt=open(p).read()\nt=t.replace(\"v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..GDScript).\",\"v=3 used parent T1059 (C#..JSP).\")\ns=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); js=t.index('```json',s); je=t.index('```',js+7)\nold=json.loads(t[js+7:je])\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in old}\nprose='''## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D22 nights (see git history) and D23 night\nlyr-tag-layer-peel, corpus-stage-correlation, game-script-language-route, godot-resource-pck-carrier,\nlinux-package-maintainer-scripts. Given up (2 attempts): python-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router,\nfile-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks, macos-pkg-installer-scripts. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to\nhctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/Evtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; REJECTED so far: csv,\nast, shlex, marshal, pathlib, pickletools -- use os.path and hand-rolled parsers) and the lane fixture test's 2 s\nfind_codecs budget. Priority-1 order for D25: the per-file timed grammar in lib (still the timed contract on D24), then the\nD24 next_language pool languages most likely next (JVM siblings beanshell/kotlin after JSP; BEAM erlang/elixir with the new\n`%` comment char; zsh/fish shell twins; awk/sed), then the JSP/webshell twists, then leftovers.\n\n'''\nnew=[\n dict(keep['per-file-hashed-contract'], detail=keep['per-file-hashed-contract']['detail']+\" RETRY NOTE (D23 night failed): tests/test_lane_fixtures.py script/nested_msbuild_entities.json made find_codecs take 2.06 s (> 2 s budget) -- keep new detectors gated on cheap substring tests and do not widen find_codecs; put pf_route/pf_answer beside it. D24 TT 1c3f64b8 / Mastery 2afec5c3 (8 sets) are further GM-verified cases with the same grammar.\"),\n {\"id\":\"next-lang-pool-polyglot-battery\",\"concept\":\"fixture battery for every language left in the timed next_language pool (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23's timed pool contained jsp and D24 shipped JSP (pool then dropped jsp). Template = the D24 JSP shape: line-1 comment marker `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG|LYR-..>-<data>` in the language's comment syntax (`#` awk/sed/tcl/zsh/fish/elixir/nim/terraform/make/docker, `%` erlang, `//` kotlin/beanshell/swift/rust/terraform, `<!-- -->` xslt) + one descriptor literal in the language's const form + an inert return. Build 4 polyglots (benign-utility/downloader/launcher/staged-chain) + one plausible host per language (e.g. kotlin gradle_kts, beanshell jmeter/bsh_servlet, xslt msxsl/wmic_format, terraform local_exec, makefile/dockerfile build) under BOTH id grammars (single `polyglot-<lang>-<role>-<field>`; timed `polyglot-<lang>-<6hex>-<field>` with url-host/path-leaf/campaign-token). Assert lib.codec.v3_plan + plan_answer return every field; campaign `<LANG_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid` (underscores kept: terraform_hcl).\"},\n {\"id\":\"kotlin-beanshell-literal-route\",\"concept\":\"JVM siblings of D20 Groovy / D24 JSP: Kotlin `.kts` and BeanShell `.bsh` descriptor literals and folds\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Both in the pool; the lane pairs siblings (AutoIt->AHK, Jenkins->GHA, Groovy->JSP). Kotlin: `const val DESCRIPTOR_X = \\\"..\\\"`, `val x: String = \\\"..\\\"`, raw `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` with `${'$'}` escapes and `.trimIndent()`, `buildString { append(..) }`, `listOf(..).joinToString(\\\"\\\")`, `\\\\uXXXX`; BeanShell: loose `descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";` or `String descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\";`, `source(\\\"..\\\")`, `exec(\\\"..\\\")`, `+` concatenation across lines. Java unicode escapes `\\\\u0022` are processed before lexing -- unescape then rescan. Fold to one literal before V3 peel; T1059 parent.\"},\n {\"id\":\"beam-erlang-elixir-route\",\"concept\":\"Erlang `.erl`/escript and Elixir `.ex`/`.exs` carriers (first `%` comment marker)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Erlang: `%% HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` comments, `-module(x).`, `-define(DESCRIPTOR_X, \\\"..\\\").`, `descriptor_x() -> \\\"..\\\".`, binaries `<<\\\"..\\\">>` and int-list binaries `<<118,61,51>>` / charlists `[118,61,51]` (decimal -> bytes), `++` concat, escript `#!/usr/bin/env escript`, exec primitives `os:cmd/1`, `open_port({spawn,..})`. Elixir: `# ` comments, `defmodule X do`, module attribute `@descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` (NO `=`), sigils `~s(..)` `~S\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"` `~c\\\"..\\\"`, `<>` concat, `System.cmd/2`, `Base.decode64!/1`. Teach lib.codec.v3_plan the `%` marker line and these descriptor forms; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n {\"id\":\"zsh-fish-shell-route\",\"concept\":\"zsh and fish shell carriers (and a possible `zsh-advanced`/`fish-advanced` Feature_ set like bash-advanced)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"zsh: `typeset -r DESCRIPTOR_X=\\\"..\\\"`, `readonly`, parameter-expansion flags `${(j::)arr}` (join), `${(s:,:)x}` (split), `${(Oa)arr}` (reverse array), `${(%)..}`, `print -r --`, `$'..'` ANSI-C, `zmodload zsh/net/tcp`, persistence `.zshenv`/`.zshrc` (T1546.004). fish: `set -g/-l/-x descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` (no `=`), `string join '' $parts`, `string split`, `function ..; end`, `begin; end`, `(cmd)` substitution, `config.fish`/`conf.d` persistence. Static emulation of the join/split/reverse flags (never run a shell); if Feature_-style fixtures appear, feature/primitive plan-verbatim as bash-advanced (role advanced_syntax, T1059.004).\"},\n {\"id\":\"awk-sed-program-route\",\"concept\":\"awk and sed programs as carriers (string juxtaposition, sprintf char codes, sed `y///` transliteration and `s///e`)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"awk: `#!/usr/bin/awk -f`, `BEGIN { descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\" }`, concatenation by JUXTAPOSITION (`\\\"ab\\\" \\\"cd\\\"` or `a b`), `sprintf(\\\"%c\\\", n)` char-code loops, `split()`+loop joins, `-v x=..` on a shebang/cmd line, exec primitives `system()`, `\\\"cmd\\\" | getline`, `print | \\\"sh\\\"`. sed: `#!/bin/sed -f`, descriptor as the replacement of `s/^/<data>/`, `i\\\\`/`a\\\\` text, `y/abc/xyz/` (a substitution CODEC -- apply it), GNU `s/../../e` and `e cmd` exec, `w /path`. Static only: never run awk/sed on fixtures (BEGIN runs on lint).\"},\n {\"id\":\"jsp-jspx-unicode-carrier\",\"concept\":\"JSP carrier twists: JSPX XML syntax, Java unicode escapes, includes across members\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"A timed/Mastery or host twist of D24: JSPX `<jsp:root xmlns:jsp=..>` with `<jsp:declaration>private static final String DESCRIPTOR_X = &quot;..&quot;;</jsp:declaration>` (XML entities, CDATA), `<jsp:scriptlet>`, `<jsp:expression>`; Java `\\\\uXXXX` escapes anywhere in source (even `\\\\u002f\\\\u002f` comment openers); `<%@ include file=\\\"x.jspf\\\" %>` / `<jsp:include page=..>` pulling the descriptor from another member (resolve per Mastery set); `.tag`/`.tagx` files; `WEB-INF/web.xml` servlet mapping; `.war` = zip -> recurse. lib: jsp_text(data) -> normalised Java text (entities + unicode escapes + include splice) before v3_plan.\"},\n {\"id\":\"webshell-request-primitive-model\",\"concept\":\"webshell request/stage order and real-vs-inert execution primitives (D24 prompt; never asked yet)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 asked to 'recover the order of requests and stages, then separate the inert fixture behavior from the lines that would be real execution primitives' but shipped no handler code (D8 php_webshell, D19 ASPX, D20 classic ASP likewise). If a host ever ships it: lib.codec.webshell_model(text, lang) -> {requests: [param/header names in source order], stages: [ordered plan/code stages], primitives: [(line_no, api, kind exec|eval|class_load|file_write|net|deserialize, live: bool)]}. API tables: JSP request.getParameter/getHeader/getInputStream, Runtime.getRuntime().exec, ProcessBuilder.start, ScriptEngineManager.getEngineByName(..).eval, ClassLoader.defineClass, Class.forName(..).newInstance, ObjectInputStream.readObject, FileOutputStream; PHP $_GET/$_POST/$_REQUEST/$_COOKIE/getallheaders + system/exec/passthru/shell_exec/proc_open/popen/eval/assert/create_function/preg_replace-e/include; ASPX Request[..]/Request.Form + Process.Start/Assembly.Load; ASP Request.Form + WScript.Shell Run/Exec, Execute/Eval; CFM cfexecute. live=false when inside a comment, a string literal, `if (false)`/dead branch or after a `return`. ATT&CK T1505.003 (web shell) alongside the plan's own attack.\"},\n {\"id\":\"nim-swift-tcl-literal-route\",\"concept\":\"Nim, Swift and Tcl string-literal forms that can hide the descriptor\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"All in the pool. Nim: `# ` / `#[ ]#` comments, `const descriptorX = \\\"..\\\"`, `let`, raw `r\\\"..\\\"`, `\\\"\\\"\\\"..\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `&` concat, `\\\\x41` escapes, `import osproc` + `execProcess`/`startProcess`. Swift: `#!/usr/bin/swift`, `//` + `/* */`, `let descriptor_x: String = \\\"..\\\"`, raw `#\\\"..\\\"#`, multi-line `\\\"\\\"\\\"`, `\\\\u{41}`, `String(decoding: bytes, as: UTF8.self)`, `Process()`/`launchPath`. Tcl: `# ` comments (only at command start), `set descriptor_x \\\"..\\\"` / `set descriptor_x {..}` (no `=`), `append`, `binary decode base64`/`hex`, `[join $l \\\"\\\"]`, `exec`. Fold, then V3 peel; fixtures in both grammars.\"},\n dict(keep['composite-label-field-regime'], detail=keep['composite-label-field-regime']['detail']+\" RETRY NOTE (D23 night failed): `import pathlib` is not an allowed lib import -- use os.path/os.listdir.\"),\n dict(keep['game-archive-carriers'], priority=3, detail=keep['game-archive-carriers']['detail']+\" RETRY NOTE (D23 night failed): `import pickletools` is not allowed -- hand-parse the pickle opcodes needed (PROTO, FRAME, EMPTY_DICT/LIST, MARK, BINUNICODE/SHORT_BINUNICODE, BINBYTES, BININT*, LONG1, TUPLE*, SETITEMS, APPENDS, STOP) and reject everything else. Game thread cooled on D24 (JSP), hence priority 3.\"),\n]\nnotes=[]\nfor g in old:\n    if g['action']=='prebuild': continue\n    g=dict(g)\n    if g['id']=='mastery-set-scope': g['detail']+=\" D24: stems identical across all 8 sets again (`588efb.jsp` set1..set8) with set-distinct plans; the D23 per-set fix held (Mastery 2afec5c3 first try).\"\n    if g['id']=='timed-contract-shape-diff': g['detail']+=\" D24: the per-file grammar persisted unchanged (TT 1560 = 1495 + 65 jsp ids; 0 generalize workers); keep the check, it now guards the NEXT reshape.\"\n    if g['id']=='solver-lib-v3-fallback': g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\"STILL OPEN after D22: the D22 solve.py (byte-identical D21 copy)\",\"STILL OPEN after D24: the D24 solve.py (byte-identical D23 copy)\")\n    if g['id']=='leaf-ext-list': g['detail']=g['detail'].replace(\".nsi .gd (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp\",\".nsi .gd .jsp (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .bsh .erl .ex .exs .nim .swift .fish .zsh\")\n    if g['id']=='family-name-underscore': g['detail']+=\" D24: `polyglot-jsp` (campaign JSP-, url host jsp-.., file_path /tmp/huntress-jsp/..) + host `host-jsp-webshell-jsp` (profile jsp_webshell); in TIMED the host folds into `polyglot-jsp` (5 members).\"\n    notes.append(g)\nnotes.insert(0,{\"id\":\"next-language-pool-roadmap\",\"concept\":\"read the timed plans' next_language pool as the forecast of upcoming languages\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D23 timed pool = 17 never-shipped languages incl. jsp; D24 shipped JSP and its timed pool lost exactly jsp (16 left: awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh). Each night: collect next_language values from the day's auto-time_trial/auto-mastery expected.json; the language that disappeared is tomorrow's already-shipped one, the rest are the queue. One data point so far -- re-verify after D25.\"})\ngaps=new+notes\nbody=json.dumps(gaps, ensure_ascii=False, indent=None)\nlines=[\"[\"]+[\"  \"+json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False)+(\",\" if i<len(gaps)-1 else \"\") for i,g in enumerate(gaps)]+[\"]\"]\nt=t[:s]+prose+\"```json\\n\"+\"\\n\".join(lines)+\"\\n\"+t[je:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\nt=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/script-analysis.md').read()\ns=t.index('## Readiness gaps'); js=t.index('```json',s); je=t.index('```',js+7)\ng=json.loads(t[js+7:je]); st=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nassert all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g)\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not (st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('ok') in (True,'True') or int(st.get('script-analysis:'+x['id'],{}).get('attempts',0))>=2)]\nprint(len(g), 'pending prebuild', len(pend), pend)\nprint(len(set(x['id'] for x in g))==len(g))\nEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md; wc -l reference/coverage/script-analysis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_read_input_tokens":130618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1783},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"278d30c6-8338-440c-a01b-243a15881645","uuid":"96004ed7-29ce-4021-9d15-03fe2ee37fda","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:27:10.853Z","request_id":"